<!--
script.md — verbatim spoken script, routed to slides.

Authored at Stage 5, after the visual deck has been signed off. Until then,
the spoken frame lives inline on each slide as a SPEAKER NOTES /
TRANSITION IN / TRANSITION OUT comment block; this file does not exist.
At Stage 5, scaffold this file with `tools/script_format.py --init`, migrate
the inline blocks into ## @<selector> blocks here, and delete the inline
blocks from slides.md.

Each block:
    ## @<selector>[, @<selector>...]
    <prose>

Selectors:
  - @slug                     one slide (id matches a slide in slides.md)
  - @slug-a..slug-b           inclusive range in slides.md document order
  - @a, @c..e, @g             multiple selectors, comma-separated

The block's prose becomes the speaker notes for every slide in its selection,
so a single block can cover a continuous narrative spanning several builds.

Conventions inside blocks:
  - (right-arrow) is a presenter rehearsal cue. Compiler ignores it.
  - (play) marks an in-slide video trigger. Compiler ignores it.
  - Author-only notes use a `<!-- @ ... -->` HTML comment where `@` is the
    first non-whitespace character after the opening `<!--`. These are
    stripped silently at compile time. Plain `<!-- ... -->` comments are
    preserved.

To scaffold this file after writing slides.md, run:

    uv run tools/script_format.py --init --force

That writes one block per slide with `TODO:` placeholders, in slides.md order.
Then merge adjacent blocks into ranges where the narrative flows continuously
across builds.

Delete this header comment and replace with your first block, e.g.:

    ## @your-first-slide-id

    Opening sentence; ABT statement.
-->
